+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | In Progress          |
+
+`ToolRegistry` in `src/orchestration/tools/registry.ts` validates every tool call's `input` against the resolved `ToolDefinition.inputSchema` (`src/types/ai.ts`) before invoking the tool's executor. Validation turns malformed model calls into value-redacted `ToolResponse` values that the model can read and correct within its tool-round budget rather than reaching executors unchecked or aborting the conversation stream.
+
+## Schema compilation
+
+- Registering a static `ToolDefinition` compiles its `inputSchema` once at `register` time and throws synchronously with a message naming the tool when the schema cannot be compiled ([validated by: throws at registration time naming the tool when a static schema cannot be compiled](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L83)).
+- A static tool's `inputSchema` is compiled once at registration and reused across subsequent `execute` calls rather than recompiled per call.
+- Registering a function-valued `ToolDefinitionSource` resolves its definition on each `execute` call and validates `input` against the `inputSchema` returned for that call rather than a stale schema from an earlier call, caching compiled validators by resolved schema object ([validated by: validates a function-valued tool definition against the schema current at each call](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L98)).
+
+## Input validation and failure boundary
+
+- `ToolRegistry.execute` checks `input` against `required`, declared types, and `enum` on the resolved `inputSchema` before invoking the executor; when validation fails it returns a `ToolResponse` whose `result` describes the failure without calling the executor, and when validation succeeds it passes `input` through unchanged — preserving unlisted extra properties without injecting `additionalProperties: false`, coercing types, or applying schema defaults ([validated by: enforces required and enum on execute while passing extra keys through unchanged](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L15)).
+- Rejection `result` text and emitted `log` lines (`src/shared/logger.ts`) name the failing property paths and the constraint that failed, and never include any input property value, so rejected payloads carrying wrong-typed or identifying fields leak no caller data into model context or logs ([validated by: names failing paths and expected types while redacting values from results and logs](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L45)).
+- `ToolRegistry.execute` throws `Unknown tool: <name>` only when no tool is registered under `name`; schema rejection never throws, and there is no opt-out flag per tool or per call.
+
+## Orchestrator retry loop
+
+- Because a schema rejection returns a `ToolResponse` rather than throwing, `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts` feeds the rejection `result` back to the provider as a `tool_result` message on the next round so the model can correct the call and `processMessage` resolves within the configured `maxToolRounds` bound ([validated by: feeds a schema rejection back through the orchestrator loop so retry resolves](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L137)).
